[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 803,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 607,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123054,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 607,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nodular ganglioneuroblastoma (GNBn; composite Schwannian stroma&ndash;rich/dominant and Schwannian stroma&ndash;poor) is composed of distinct histologies (clones): intermixed ganglioneuroblastoma (GNBi) or ganglioneuroma and neuroblastoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 804,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 608,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123055,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 608,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9490/3 Ganglioneuroblastoma, nodular</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 805,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 609,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123056,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 609,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2A00.21 &amp; XH77W7 Mixed neuronal-glial tumours &amp; Ganglioneuroblastoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 806,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 610,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123057,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 610,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 807,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 611,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123058,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 611,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 808,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 612,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123059,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 612,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Primary GNBn occurs in sites associated with neural crest migration, including the adrenal medulla {14601099; 10964346}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 809,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 613,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123060,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 613,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Adrenal GNBn is detected as a suprarenal mass {22137163; 28465480}. Occasionally, metastatic disease leads to the diagnosis {14601099}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 810,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 614,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123061,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 614,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GNBn is uncommon, accounting for 8% of all peripheral neuroblastic tumours filed at the Children&rsquo;s Oncology Group (COG) Neuroblastoma Pathology Reference Laboratory. It is rare in infancy, and the majority of cases are diagnosed in children aged &gt;&nbsp;18&nbsp;months {22137163}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 811,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 615,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123062,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 615,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 812,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 616,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123063,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 616,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GNBn has multiple components, i.e. GNBi or ganglioneuroma (biologically favourable with advanced tumour maturation) and neuroblastoma (either biologically favourable or unfavourable with less tumour maturation) in a single mass. These are considered to represent different clones rather than focal maturation or dedifferentiation {14601099; 10964346}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 819,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 623,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123064,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 623,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The neuroblastoma component, often haemorrhagic and necrotic, is typically a discrete nodule in a background of GNBi/ganglioneuroma that is solid/firm and white/yellow. Multiple nodules may be present. Sampling of all nodules for histopathological and molecular evaluation is critical for case management. The proportion of neuroblastoma and GNBi/ganglioneuroma in an individual tumour varies case by case.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 813,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 617,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123065,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 617,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Diagnosis requires the identification of GNBi/ganglioneuroma and neuroblastoma in a single tumour. The neuroblastoma nodule is separated from the GNBi/ganglioneuroma by a fibrous capsule, a pushing border without a definite capsule, or an infiltrative margin. Rarely, a primary site biopsy shows GNBi/ganglioneuroma with neuroblastoma detected in a metastatic site. The neuroblastic differentiation, grade, and mitosis-karyorrhexis index of each neuroblastoma nodule is essential, with categorization as &ldquo;favourable histology&rdquo; or &ldquo;unfavourable histology&rdquo; according to the International Neuroblastoma Pathology Classification (INPC; see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/53/102\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Neuroblastoma</em>).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 814,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 618,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123066,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 618,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytopathological smears are similar to those of GNBi {31231909}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 815,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 619,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123067,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 619,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Genomic/molecular investigation is focused on the neuroblastoma component (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/53/102\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Neuroblastoma</em>). <em>MYCN</em> amplification is rare (2%) {22137163}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 818,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 622,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123068,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 622,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> distinct histologies (clones) of GNBi/ganglioneuroma and neuroblastoma; assessment of the neuroblastoma component as per the INPC criteria.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> genomic/molecular testing of the neuroblastoma component.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 816,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 620,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123069,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 620,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The International Neuroblastoma Risk Group Staging System (INRGSS) is recommended for clinical staging based on the presence or absence of image-defined risk factors {19047290}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 817,
    "bookid": 53,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 621,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 123070,
        "bookId": 53,
        "chapterId": 104,
        "headingId": 621,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis for patients with GNBn is determined by the clinical, histopathological, and molecular characteristics of the neuroblastoma component {14601099; 22137163; 28465480} (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/53/102\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Neuroblastoma</em>).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-10-09T12:55:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]